  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115642",
      "title": "Class Bindings: Repetition",
      "lectureOrder": 119,
      "videoOrder": 113,
      "sourceHash": "054db2a21aec7dd173bb77ef213c6e7f19c77ca9c9bf8c423581e007995ab572",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.27,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "Maybe you recall that in the server status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 8.6,
          "en": "component CSS file, there are some CSS selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "which don't select anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 14.13,
          "en": "because I'm looking for a CSS class status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.13,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "or status online or offline.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 21.273,
          "en": "And in that template, those classes don't exist anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.23,
          "end": 24.45,
          "en": "Instead, what we have in this template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.45,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "is some conditional check with the @if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "about which you learned earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "combined with 'else if' to check for an additional condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "and 'else' to render something that will be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.07,
          "en": "if none of these conditions is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.07,
          "end": 43.413,
          "en": "But we don't have those CSS classes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 49.61,
          "en": "Now, my idea with those classes is to add them conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "to an element here in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "just as we're outputting some elements conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 61.56,
          "en": "Now, to make that work and to actually see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 63.84,
          "en": "that some things rendered conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.84,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "or some class is added conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "we, first of all, need to tweak",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 71.43299999999999,
          "en": "that server status component, TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "Because in there, I got this current status property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 78.423,
          "en": "and at the moment, it's always set to online.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "Now, my idea with this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 86.75,
          "en": "is that it should reflect a changing server status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "Now of course, this is just a dummy application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 94.72999999999999,
          "en": "so we don't actually grab any real server status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 99.3,
          "en": "but I at least wanna change the current server status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.3,
          "end": 102.81,
          "en": "every couple of seconds, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.81,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "I wanna randomly change it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "from online to offline or to unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 112.91,
          "en": "These are the three different status values I wanna support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "Therefore, what I'll do here is I'll bring back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "a wrapping div because it's on that div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 123.36,
          "en": "where I wanna add some clause conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.36,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "And we can then add a clause conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 129.93,
          "en": "or set the clause value dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.93,
          "end": 134.93,
          "en": "with help of Angular's class binding, which looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "You can bind the class property on a div dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 142.413,
          "en": "by using this property binding syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "But under the hood, Angular then actually detects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "that it's the class you're binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 154.61,
          "en": "and it then extends the default property binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 158.97,
          "en": "for this class property, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.97,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "For example, if you would want to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "the status class conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "you could do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 170.46,
          "en": "You could set class.status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.46,
          "end": 173.61,
          "en": "and then for example check if current status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 173.61,
          "end": 176.673,
          "en": "equals offline, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "Now, the status class would only be applied to that div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 184.473,
          "en": "if this condition is met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.61,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "and that is a syntax you saw earlier in the course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 194.19,
          "en": "that you can add or remove classes dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.19,
          "end": 196.293,
          "en": "with help of this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 202.11,
          "en": "So here in this case where server status is online,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 202.11,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "this check here will actually produce false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 209.013,
          "en": "and the status class will not be added to this div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 210.51,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "As a result, if you save that and you reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "and you then inspect that server status component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 220.44,
          "en": "you'll see that div in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.44,
          "end": 224.88,
          "en": "this div here inside of the app server status component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 224.88,
          "end": 226.893,
          "en": "but there is no class on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "Now, if I change my check to check for online",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 233.94,
          "en": "and will soon make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "that this actually changes dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 238.86,
          "en": "for the moment, I'll leave it hardcoded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 238.86,
          "end": 241.62,
          "en": "But if I check for online and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 241.62,
          "end": 243.813,
          "en": "you'll see that this class is added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 249.51,
          "en": "So that's how you can add or set classes dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 252.72,
          "en": "with help of Angular's class-binding feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 255.72,
          "en": "But that is a syntax you already knew.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 255.72,
          "end": 257.58,
          "en": "Now, we'll dig a bit deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 260.43,
          "en": "and see how else you could use this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.43,
          "end": 262.743,
          "en": "in ways you didn't know about yet.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
